{
 "title": "Bayesian Parametric Portfolio Policies",
 "hypothesis": "Factors are timed as a portfolio rule: the covariance between portfolio weights and subsequent factor returns is positive after imposing position and leverage limits, and survives averaging over policy uncertainty.",
 "data_sources": [
  "Ken French Data Library: monthly returns on Mkt, SMB, HML, CMA, RMW, UMD and 1-month T-bill rate",
  "Chen-Zimmermann 2022 Open Source Asset Pricing: 212 anomaly portfolio returns",
  "30 factor-specific predictors (TS-mom, CS-mom, valuation, reversal, volatility for each of 6 series) = 242 predictors + constant"
 ],
 "sample": "Monthly factor returns July 1963 to December 2023. First 121 months burn-in only for estimation. Evaluation (OOS) August 1973 to December 2023, 605 months, rolling 120-month estimation window re-estimated each month, held 1 month. Predictors standardised using only data available at date, winsorised at 3 SD, missing set to 0. Market weight always 1, benchmark factor weights 0. No historical vintage reconstruction; predictor set assembled after the fact. Filters and costs in method.",
 "period_start": "July 1963",
 "period_end": "December 2023",
 "method": [
  "1. Universe K=6 series (Mkt+5 factors SMB,HML,CMA,RMW,UMD). Investor holds w_m,t=1 + w_t'F_{t+1}, F = 5 zero-investment factor returns. Portfolio return r_{p,t+1}=r_{m,t+1}+w_t'F_{t+1}.",
  "2. Predictors z_t = [1, 242 standardised predictors] so L=243. Policy w_{k,t}(theta)=Pi_c(theta_k'z_t) for k=1..5, Pi_c(u)=min(c,max(-c,u)) with c=0.6, theta KxL =1,215 coefficients. Gross exposure limit g=1.5: if sum|w_k|>g scale down proportionally. Constant allocation imposes both limits jointly during optimisation.",
  "3. Training criterion affine surrogate q_s(theta)=1+r_{m,s+1}+ sum_k theta_k'z_s F_{k,s+1}. Utility CRRA U(q)=(q^{1-gamma}-1)/(1-gamma) gamma=5. Prior theta_{k,l}~N(0, lambda_l^{-1}), lambda0=delta_s^{-2} delta_s=0.8, lambda_{l>=1}=(L-1)delta_tau^{-2} delta_tau=1. Criterion f(theta)= -omega sum_{s in T_t} U(q_s(theta)) +0.5 theta'Lambda theta, T_t=120 months ending t-1. Penalised version f_kappa adds omega*kappa/2 sum_{s>min} sum_k phi_k[theta_k'(z_s-z_{s-1})]^2.",
  "4. Learning rate omega via diagonal trace-matching: omega_t = sum H_{jj}^{-1}/ sum V_{jj}H_{jj}^{-2} over j with H_{jj}>xi, V Bartlett long-run variance. Compute mode at provisional rate, re-evaluate omega_t, recompute mode at omega_t. Median omega 5.80. Newton from alpha=0 on kernel K_{ss'}=(F_{s+1}'F_{s'+1})(z_s'Lambda_L^{-1}z_{s'}) etc., backtracking, bound f(theta)-min <=0.5 rho'K rho =0.5 nabla'Lambda^{-1}nabla.",
  "5. Portfolios: RPPP w^{RPPP}_{k,t}=Pi_c(hat theta_{k,t}'z_t). BPPP w^{BPPP}_{k,t}=E[Pi_c(theta_k'z_t)] under Laplace N(hat theta_t,C_t), closed form -c Phi(a)+ mu[Phi(b)-Phi(a)]+ sigma[phi(a)-phi(b)]+c[1-Phi(b)], a=(-c-mu)/sigma,b=(c-mu)/sigma, sigma^2=z_t'C_{kk,t}z_t via Woodbury sigma^2= z'Lambda_L^{-1}z - h'(D^{-1}+K)^{-1}h, D=omega gamma diag(q^{-gamma-1}), h_{k,s}=F_{k,s+1}z_s'Lambda_L^{-1}z_t. Then gross-scale if needed. Exact posterior sampled in rank(K)<=T via HMC on u=G theta~N(0,K): 32 chains, 300 burn-in, 700 retained, 12 steps size 0.3 whitened, seeds 1-12, rank 113-119 first 7 windows, min rank 113.",
  "6. Comparators same limits, re-estimated monthly on past data only: constant allocation maximising CRRA net of holding costs; minimum variance (120m cov); scaled minimum variance; inverse variance (60m); reward-to-risk (60m); lasso (120m regression of 1 on factor returns, penalty by hold-out Sharpe, vol-target); conditional mean-variance ridge forecast of factor returns on same 242 predictors avg 12/48m, ridge+window chosen 24m by CE. All hold market=1.",
  "7. Costs: trading phi=60,25,30,30,70 bps for SMB,HML,CMA,RMW,UMD; holding h=90,40,45,45,80 bps annual on |w|, charged monthly divided by 12. Market no cost, initial purchase not charged. Net r^n = r_m+w'F - sum phi|dw| - sum h|w|.",
  "8. Statistics: Sharpe sqrt12*mean/sd total and excess over T-bill; CE=12[(T^{-1}sum(1+r_p)^{1-gamma})^{1/(1-gamma)}-1]; turnover 12*avg sum|dw|; exposure avg sum|w|; timing decomposition E[w_kF_k]=E[w_k]E[F_k]+Cov(w_k,F_k) summed over 5 factors, share timing/active, divisor T, Newey-West Bartlett bw floor(4(T/100)^{2/9})=5 at T=605. Paired Sharpe diff via Ledoit-Wolf 2008 delta HAC, Holm correction. Robustness grids: prior scales {0.4,0.8,1.6}x{0.5,1.0,1.5} by past OOS CE; penalty kappa in {0,5,10,20,40,80,160,320,640} with 3x3x3 grid recursively; bagged ridge 100 circular block bootstrap 12m; PCA on predictors re-estimated each date sign-fixed."
 ],
